<div class="page-head"><div><h1>Help &amp; glossary</h1><p>How the hub works, in plain words.</p></div></div>
<div class="grid-half">
  <section class="card"><div class="card-head"><h2>Stock words</h2></div><div class="card-body"><dl class="kv">
    <dt>On hand</dt><dd>Every unit physically in the Delhi warehouse, including damaged units and returns waiting to be checked.</dd>
    <dt>Reserved</dt><dd>Units held for orders that have been placed but not yet dispatched. They are on the shelf but already sold.</dd>
    <dt>Available</dt><dd>What the storefronts can sell: on hand − reserved − damaged − awaiting inspection.</dd>
    <dt>Incoming</dt><dd>Units on purchase orders that have not arrived. They are never counted as available.</dd>
    <dt>Damaged</dt><dd>Units kept aside because they cannot be sold. Write them off when they leave the building.</dd>
    <dt>Awaiting inspection</dt><dd>Customer returns that have arrived but not been checked. They become available only when someone approves them for resale.</dd>
    <dt>Reorder level</dt><dd>When available stock drops below this number, the product shows as Low stock and one alert is sent until it is restocked.</dd>
  </dl></div></section>
  <section class="card"><div class="card-head"><h2>Shared stock</h2></div><div class="card-body stack">
    <p>A product sold by more than one brand uses one stock record. An order on any storefront takes units from the same shelf, so the same unit can never be sold twice.</p>
    <p>Stock is only shared when someone links a storefront product to a SKU and confirms it. Products are never linked because their names or photos look alike.</p>
    <p>Each badge on a product tells you which case it is: <b>Shared across brands</b>, <b>One storefront</b> or <b>Not linked yet</b>.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="card"><div class="card-head"><h2>Processing an order</h2></div><div class="card-body"><ol class="stack">
    <li><b>Start processing</b> — the order joins the pick list.</li>
    <li><b>Mark as picked</b> once the items are off the shelf.</li>
    <li><b>Mark as packed</b> once the parcel is sealed.</li>
    <li><b>Create shipment</b> — choose the carrier and service. Add the tracking number from the carrier.</li>
    <li><b>Mark as dispatched</b> when the carrier collects it. Stock is deducted and the customer is told.</li>
  </ol><p class="muted mt-12">The page always shows the next step at the top. Steps that do not apply yet are not offered.</p></div></section>
  <section class="card"><div class="card-head"><h2>Payments, cancellations and refunds</h2></div><div class="card-body stack">
    <p>Payments are handled by each storefront's payment provider. The hub never marks an order as paid or refunded by itself.</p>
    <p>When you cancel an order or request a refund here, the request goes to the storefront, which runs it through the payment provider. The order changes once the storefront confirms.</p>
    <p>Returned items go to <b>Awaiting inspection</b>. They are only for sale again after someone approves them.</p>
  </div></section>
</div>
